#. translators: %s: detected third-party currency switcher plugin name(s).
#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:617
#, php-format
msgid "Another currency switcher is active. Universal Multicurrency has detected %s, which also converts WooCommerce prices."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:624
msgid "Why this is unsafe."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:627
msgid "Two plugins converting the same price multiply their rates. WooCommerce reads a product's price once, and each switcher converts whatever the previous one returned. Which runs first depends on hook priority, so the result can differ between the catalogue, the cart, and the order that is finally saved."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:634
msgid "What you may see."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:637
msgid "Prices that differ between the shop page and the cart; totals that change on reload; orders stored with a currency or rate the shopper never saw; a payment gateway charging in a different currency to the order; refunds that do not reconcile against the original total."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:644
msgid "How to resolve."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:648
msgid "Keep one. Deactivate the other switcher, then clear your object cache and WooCommerce transients. Existing orders are unaffected — each stores its own currency and exchange rate permanently."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:653
msgid "Ask an administrator to deactivate the other switcher, then clear your object cache and WooCommerce transients. Existing orders are unaffected — each stores its own currency and exchange rate permanently."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:661
msgid "Contact your network administrator if you cannot deactivate plugins yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/ConflictNotice.php:665
msgid "Universal Multicurrency will not change, disable, or deactivate any other plugin."
msgstr ""

